  "footnotes": [
    "Decision configs: 'default' = tau .5 / AND-gate / median k3 / persistence 2 (historical). 'val-tuned' = selected on the 62-clip val split by binary F1 (persistence by val EDS), frozen, applied once to test. R5-R7 reuse R4's frozen gate so the only variable is the prompt/graph conditioning.",
    "MistSense's originally reported 0.495 used a tau sweep ON TEST (oracle selection) over 872 coarse windows; R8/R9 replace it with val-selected tau. The oracle number is retained here for transparency, not comparison.",
    "Zero-shot rows: auc_raw ~= 0.48 (chance) \u2014 the tuned zero-shot F1 reflects threshold placement on a near-chance ranker, and its high EDS reflects indiscriminate early firing (see EDS footnote).",
    "R7 and R10 were pre-registered and cancelled without being run: both decompose a detection effect, and R5/R6 established there is none to decompose. Their row files do not exist and the builder skips them.",
    "R12 is the trivial always-fire detector, re-gated through the identical decision layer for comparability. Its auc_raw is 0.5 by construction (a constant score cannot rank).",
    "R11 corrects the step-assignment rule on BOTH sides (gold-step teacher forcing in training, rate-limited causal pointer at eval). It cuts saturation from 66% to 20.7% of windows and still fails: the causal pointer agrees with the gold step on 7.7% of windows, so a model trained on always-correct steps is out of distribution and fires on 93%.",
    "Protocol: online causal, clip_len 4s, stride 4s, fps 1; trailing <stride s per clip unsampled (floor tiling).",
    "69 nonlocalizable (start=-1, mostly Missing-Step) segments mark NO window and are unrecallable by windowed metrics; 1 'Other'-only step(s) dropped from typed metrics. missing_step is structurally unreachable -> macro_f1_excl_missing_step.",
    "CIs: clip-level bootstrap, n=1000, seed=0, percentile 95%. Windows within a clip are correlated; clips are the resampling unit.",
    "EDS must be read jointly with precision: a system that fires early and often scores high EDS regardless of accuracy.",
    "Localization uses min_consecutive persistence from each row's decision config; binary F1 gates on smoothed score>0 \u2014 different decision rules by design.",
    "auc_raw ranks by the raw (ungated) per-window confidence \u2014 threshold-free, comparable across rows."
  ]
}